api.github.com/users/Veradictus","html_url":"https://github.com/Veradictus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T08:02:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T08:02:35Z","body":"> [@Veradictus](https://github.com/Veradictus) On the bottom it states:\n> \n> > 2D rendering currently doesn't benefit from increased precision when large world coordinates are enabled. This can cause visible model snapping to occur when far away from the world origin (starting from a few million pixels at typical zoom levels). 2D physics calculations will still benefit from increased precision though.\n\nIt literally fixes all the aforementioned issues. The tilemap in my game does not have tearing anymore and the players are happy.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2768521949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]